  27\t| 7 | `json_object`, size/get/getn/set variants | empty/one/many; replacement; C-string and length keys; embedded-NUL key with nocheck | [ ] |\n    28\t| 8 | object delete/clear | first/middle/last/missing key, length key, empty and many objects | [ ] |\n    29\t| 9 | object update family | update all/existing/missing/recursive; disjoint, overlapping, nested keys | [ ] |\n    30\t| 10 | object iterator family | empty/one/many, iter-at, key-to-iter, next, key length/value, replace through iterator | [ ] |\n    31\t| 11 | `json_object_seed` | zero autoseed and explicit nonzero seeds before object creation | [ ] |\n    32\t| 12 | `json_array`, size/get | empty, one, many; indices zero/middle/last | [ ] |\n    33\t| 13 | array set/append/insert/remove/clear | front/middle/end, capacity growth across 8 entries | [ ] |\n    34\t| 14 | `json_array_extend` | empty/nonempty source and destination, self-extension | [ ] |\n    35\t| 15 | `json_equal` | every type; equal/unequal; nested objects with differing insertion order | [ ] |\n    36\t| 16 | `json_copy`, `json_deep_copy`, `do_deep_copy` | every scalar; shallow/deep object and array; nested structures | [ ] |\n    37\t| 17 | load entry points | `json_loads`, `json_loadb`, `json_loadf`, `json_loadfd`, `json_load_file`, `json_load_callback` with object/array | [ ] |\n    38\t| 18 | load input shape | empty object/array, nested, empty/one/many members, whitespace, all scalar token types | [ ] |\n    39\t| 19 | load string shape | escapes, control escapes, BMP/non-BMP Unicode escapes, raw multibyte UTF-8 | [ ] |\n    40\t| 20 | load number shape | integer extrema, `-0`, decimal, exponent signs/cases, finite real boundaries | [ ] |\n    41\t| 21 | load flags | no flags vs `JSON_DECODE_ANY` for scalar top-level values | [ ] |\n    42\t| 22 | load flags | `JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES` off/on with duplicate and unique keys | [ ] |\n    43\t| 23 | load flags | `JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK` off/on with trailing JSON tokens/text | [ ] |\n    44\t| 24 | load flags | `JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL` off/on for integer tokens | [ ] |\n    45\t| 25 | load flags | `JSON_ALLOW_NUL` off/on for `\\u0000` in values; NUL keys remain rejected | [ ] |\n    46\t| 26 | load flags | meaningful combinations/cross-product of the five decode flags | [ ] |\n    47\t| 27 | dump entry points | `json_dumps`, `json_dumpb`, `json_dump_callback`, `json_dumpf`, `json_dumpfd`, `json_dump_file` | [ ] |\n    48\t| 28 | dump types | object/array and every scalar with `JSON_ENCODE_ANY` off/on | [ ] |\n    49\t| 29 | dump indentation | widths 0, 1, 2, 31 on empty/one/many/nested containers | [ ] |\n    50\t| 30 | dump formatting | compact off/on crossed with indentation and nested containers | [ ] |\n    51\t| 31 | dump strings | ensure-ASCII off/on for BMP/non-BMP; escape-slash off/on; controls/quotes/backslashes | [ ] |\n    52\t| 32 | dump objects | sort-keys off/on for ASCII, prefix, case, multibyte, and embedded-NUL keys | [ ] |\n    53\t| 33 | dump order | preserve-order bit off/on (C treats it as insertion order in either state) | [ ] |\n    54\t| 34 | dump embedding | `JSON_EMBED` off/on for empty/nonempty object and array | [ ] |\n    55\t| 35 | dump real precision | precision 0 and 1..31; fixed/exponent thresholds; extrema/subnormal/random finite values | [ ] |\n    56\t| 36 | `json_dumpb` | buffer null/zero, undersized, exact, oversized; returned required byte count | [ ] |\n    57\t| 37 | pack entry points | `json_pack`, `json_pack_ex`, `json_vpack_ex` with scalar formats `s,i,I,f,b,n,o,O` | [ ] |\n    58\t| 38 | pack containers | empty/one/many/nested `{}` and `[]`; ignored spaces, tabs, newlines, commas, colons | [ ] |\n    59\t| 39 | pack strings | plain, `#`, `%`, `+`, chained concatenation, `?` and `*` optional values | [ ] |\n    60\t| 40 | pack ownership | `o`/`O` and optional variants with null/non-null values | [ ] |\n    61\t| 41 | unpack entry points | `json_unpack`, `json_unpack_ex`, `json_vunpack_ex` for `s,s%,