{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_199","type":"agent_message","text":"The remaining high-risk gap is allocation failure behavior, which affects constructors, growth paths, load/dump, pack, and hashtable internals. I’m adding a fail-switch allocator installed through each library’s exported allocator API, then exercising first-allocation and growth failures through the loaded `.so`; I’m also fixing the Rust fallback realloc-to-zero branch, which currently calls `malloc(0)` instead of freeing and returning null as C does."}}
