{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_206","type":"agent_message","text":"The allocator differential found three real mismatches: OOM during load sets a syntax code instead of leaving C’s unknown code, packed integer OOM loses `json_error_out_of_memory`, and Rust arrays never report growth failure under the installed realloc hook. I’m correcting constructor-null propagation in the parser, pack allocation errors, and array growth so it uses `jsonp_realloc` like C and respects custom allocator failure."}}
